          ],
          "overview": "Five turns (d02) examined one paper, 2004.00809 \"Mapping Languages and Demographics with Georeferenced Corpora\" — the only paper discussed, first and last. The recurring question: do the authors hypothesize why Twitter data better predicts each country's language inventory? Repeated evidence checks confirmed the finding and supporting reasons (fewer missing languages, better North America/Oceania representation) alongside candidate explanations (GDP-weighted wealthier population, urban-centered collection, commonness of English/Spanish), without any direct causal test. Unresolved references: no explicit hypothesis explains the inventory advantage, and open items remain on false-positive sources (immigration, tourism, business; Russia case) and whether rural-centered collection yields the same bias.",
